// Replace vs add a filter. Old Fin.OnLine: CALCULATE ( value, 'P&L Line'[Line ID] = "S4" ) REPLACES the
// row's line filter, so every row of a P&L matrix repeats operating profit. New Fin.OnLine wraps it in
// KEEPFILTERS: the filter is intersected with the row's line, so only the Operating profit row keeps a value.
// Expected (DuckDB, FY2013 actual, NOT run in Power BI):
//   "Replace" = 13,793,626 on every line; "KEEPFILTERS" = 13,793,626 on Operating profit, blank elsewhere.
EVALUATE
SUMMARIZECOLUMNS (
    'P&L Line'[Line],
    TREATAS ( { 2013 }, 'Date'[Year] ),
    "Replace", CALCULATE ( [Actual], 'P&L Line'[Line ID] = "S4" ),
    "KEEPFILTERS", [Operating Profit]
)
ORDER BY 'P&L Line'[Line]
